const postContent = "<h2>The Missing Money May Have Two Causes</h2>\n<p>A street committee may be waiting for contributions before paying service costs. But collecting every remaining contribution does not necessarily solve the problem. The agreed monthly budget may itself be smaller than the approved expenses.</p>\n<p>The <a href=\"/tools/community-fund-demo\">Shared Services Fund Demo</a> separates those two questions using invented references and example amounts. It is a single-period worksheet, not an accounting system, public resident register or payment service. Use synthetic examples only.</p>\n<h2>Follow The Example Without Blaming Individual Members</h2>\n<p>The sample has PKR5,000 opening unrestricted cash and PKR11,000 net agreed current contributions after a previously agreed reduction. Approved guard and cleaning costs total PKR20,000. Even after full collection, that leaves a PKR4,000 structural budget gap.</p>\n<p>At the sample's current collection stage, PKR1,500 of the agreed contributions remains unreceived. The immediate funding gap is therefore PKR5,500. Treating all of that as a collection failure would hide the underlying PKR4,000 mismatch.</p>\n<p>The cost figures are invented, not local wage rates. The example makes no claim about minimum wage, employment obligations, taxes or a committee's legal authority to collect funds.</p>\n<h2>Keep Extra Receipts Separate</h2>\n<p>One synthetic unit contributes more than its net current amount due. The excess is protected and unallocated in this worksheet. It is not automatically a donation, an approved budget increase or next month's income.</p>\n<p>Opening cash must already exclude prior advances, restricted balances and other commitments. The demo does not import earlier months or handle prior arrears. A production ledger would need allocations, refunds, reversals, period close and a clear correction history so that earlier money is not counted twice.</p>\n<h2>Reconcile Three Views</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>View</th><th>Question</th><th>What it must not imply</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Current contributions</td><td>What was agreed, reduced and received for this period?</td><td>A promise is confirmed cash</td></tr><tr><td>Cash reconciliation</td><td>What remains after recorded expense payments?</td><td>Protected advances are free to spend</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly budget</td><td>Would full agreed collection cover approved service costs?</td><td>Unpaid members caused every shortfall</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The model subtracts recorded payments once. It then compares remaining approved expenses with unrestricted cash. Negative unrestricted cash is a reconciliation warning; the report does not pretend that protected money is still available.</p>\n<p>For the invented sample, the cash trail is:</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>PKR</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Opening unrestricted cash</td><td>5,000</td><td>Entered starting balance after excluding prior restricted money</td></tr><tr><td>All receipts entered</td><td>10,500</td><td>Includes excess above current agreed dues</td></tr><tr><td>Recorded expenses paid</td><td>7,000</td><td>Deducted once from cash and approved costs</td></tr><tr><td>Calculated closing cash</td><td>8,500</td><td>Opening plus receipts minus payments</td></tr><tr><td>Protected excess receipts</td><td>1,000</td><td>Still reserved; not automatically available for services</td></tr><tr><td>Unrestricted cash</td><td>7,500</td><td>Closing cash minus protected excess</td></tr><tr><td>Approved costs still unpaid</td><td>13,000</td><td>Total approved costs of 20,000 minus 7,000 recorded as paid</td></tr><tr><td>Funding gap now</td><td>5,500</td><td>Unpaid costs minus unrestricted cash</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The download includes those balances, the net agreed contributions, the outstanding collection and the structural budget gap. It can be reviewed without opening the worksheet again. A warning appears before the amounts when unrestricted cash is negative. Even positive closing cash can be misleading if protected excess has already been spent; marking all expenses paid does not resolve a negative cash reconciliation. Check the records before interpreting a shortfall as a new request for contributions.</p>\n<h2>Share Only Reviewed Totals, Keep Member Statements Private</h2>\n<p>A committee summary should explain totals, approved costs and unresolved discrepancies without publishing an unpaid-member list. The demo's English and Urdu exports omit all member and expense references. Aggregate figures may still reveal business or household information in a small group: review the totals and intended audience before sharing. An actual private member statement would need authenticated access and clear ownership rules; a guessed identifier or shared URL is not adequate protection.</p>\n<p>The demo does not verify receipts or send reminders. “Recorded receipts entered” means that the user supplied the number, not that a bank or collector confirmed it. Both summary languages explicitly say that recorded amounts are not independently verified cash or bank balances. Do not upload resident names, phone numbers, receipts or salary records to a public demonstration.</p>\n<h2>Where AI Might Help Later</h2>\n<p>A private assistant could explain validated totals, locate authorized receipt evidence or prepare a polite reminder in the member's chosen language. An example question is: “Why is there still a gap after everyone pays?” The numeric engine would supply the answer; the assistant would explain it with links to permitted evidence.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.ollama.com/capabilities/structured-outputs\">Ollama structured outputs</a>, checked18November2026, can constrain supported self-hosted model responses to a schema. A schema does not verify a payment or grant permission to disclose a member's balance. Model extraction would still require matching and staff review. The current demo uses deterministic templates and has no model connection.</p>\n<p>A responsible assistant would not alter contributions, approve reductions, decide who is unreliable, shame members or send messages without authorization. There is no need to add an LLM to arithmetic that ordinary validated code already handles.</p>\n<h2>A Useful First Pilot</h2>\n<p>Start with one period and an agreed opening balance, contribution schedule, service budget and reviewer. Compare the report with existing records and investigate discrepancies before adding collection channels. A private live version would need role-based access, audit history, backup/recovery and a clear month-close process.</p>\n<p>Existing spreadsheets or association-management systems may already be sufficient. The reason to commission a custom integration is a specific unresolved problem: payment reconciliation, private member statements, multiple collectors or a repeatable approval workflow. Use the <a href=\"/tools/community-fund-demo\">synthetic fund worksheet</a> to identify that problem before building a larger system.</p>"

export default postContent
